<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose 11 points to 1,526.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose 11 points to 1,526.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,526 today from 1,515 on March 21, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1529    13.883	  1521    13.813</p>
<p>   1a   1562 11833.000	  1546 11713.000</p>
<p>   2    1808    25.833	  1812    25.888</p>
<p>   2a   1897 15558.000	  1894 15531.000</p>
<p>   3    1760    16.233	  1733    15.988</p>
<p>   3a   1656 13067.000	  1623 12806.000</p>
<p>   6    1239    12.779	  1236    12.750</p>
